anywhere else in America as an African-American architect. Paul Williams, African-American architect, who was much more than an African-American architect, he was simply one of the best architects of the 20th century. This is Karen Hudson, Paul Williams' biographer, and also his granddaughter. I was very close to her, my girl, a black away. Hudson says the Los Angeles, her grandfather grew up in.
可能都无法实现。保罗·威廉姆斯，这位非裔美国建筑师，其成就远不止于一位非裔美国建筑师那么简单，他简直到可以说是20世纪最伟大的建筑师之一。这位是凯伦·哈德森，保罗·威廉姆斯的传记作家，也是他的孙女。“我跟他很亲近，我是个黑皮肤女孩。”哈德森说，她祖父成长时期的洛杉矶，

