Back in the early 1900s, was pretty different from what it is now. I mean, it was open spaces. He was born downtown, Ayson, Santhip. You know downtown was a heart of LA. We were talking in 1894. And in 1894 when Williams was born Los Angeles was pretty much a small downtown surrounded with bean fields and orange groves and the wild Pacific. And the population of LA was skyrocketing. From 1890 to 1900 the city doubled from 50,000 to 100,000 residents in just 10 years.
早在20世纪初，跟现在有着很大的不同。我的意思是，那时到处都是开阔地。他在市中心出生，在一个叫……你知道的，市中心是洛杉矶的心脏。我们说的是1894年。在1894年威廉姆斯出生时，洛杉矶基本上只是一个被豆田、橘林和汹涌的太平洋环绕的小市中心。洛杉矶的人口正在飞速增长。从1890年到1900年，这座城市的人口在短短10年内翻了一番，从5万人激增至10万人。

