The growing city was full of people that had come west for a better life. Paul Williams' parents were from Memphis and had moved to Los Angeles just before he was born. They came to California for their health because they both had tuberculosis. And that's how he was orphaned before he was four. Williams was raised by foster parents. He had a brother who was nine years older than him who was raised in a different family and died at a young age of pneumonia. Without much of a family of his own, Williams spent a lot of time in the neighborhood,
这座不断扩张的城市里挤满了为了追求更好生活而来到西海岸的人们。保罗·威廉姆斯的父母来自孟菲斯，就在他出生前不久搬到了洛杉矶。他们为了健康来到加利福尼亚，因为两人都患有肺结核。这就是为什么他在四岁之前就成了孤儿。威廉姆斯是由养父母抚养长大的。他有一个比他大九岁的哥哥，被寄养在另一个家庭里，却在很小的时候就死于肺炎。由于缺乏真正的家庭关爱，威廉姆斯花了很多时间在社区里转悠，

