When his high school connections would prove very valuable in Paul Williams' career. It's hard to say exactly where Williams desired to be an architect came from. He did have a natural talent for drawing, and then somehow he learned that architecture was a profession, and then, resolutely decided it was for him, which is kind of incredible when you think about it. He never knew another architect, never really even heard of another architect when he was young. When Williams told his high school guidance counselor that he wanted to practice architecture, he was told to give it up. He should not try to be an architect.
当时他在高中时期积累的人脉在保罗·威廉姆斯的职业生涯中证明了其巨大的价值。很难说威廉姆斯想要成为建筑师的愿望究竟从何而来。他确实有着与生俱来的绘画天赋，后来不知怎的，他了解到建筑学是一门职业，然后，他坚决认定这就是他想做的事，现在想来这真是有些不可思议。他年轻时从未认识过其他建筑师，甚至从未听说过其他建筑师。当威廉姆斯告诉他高中的升学顾问自己想从事建筑行业时，对方劝他放弃。他劝他不要尝试去当建筑师。

13
00:05:45.000 --> 00:06:07.000
He should be a doctoral lawyer, because black people would always need doctors and lawyers. And white people would not hire him as an architect and black people couldn't afford him. So he should just give up. Didn't happen. Williams didn't go to architecture school. Instead, he attended different art schools and engineering school,
他应该去当一名医生或律师，因为黑人永远需要医生和律师。白人不会雇佣他当建筑师，而黑人又雇不起他。所以他还是趁早放弃吧。事实并非如此。威廉姆斯没有去读建筑学校。相反，他上了不同的艺术学校和工程学校，

