just cobbling together the skills he needed in drafting, landscaping, and materials, before he was certified as a contractor in 1915. And then came the challenge of actually getting hired. In his own notes, he said he got dressed in his best suit, and which he probably only had one for church, but best suit had his little briefcase and he went knocking on doors. He approached all the architects in the area
一点一点拼凑出他在制图、景观设计和材料学方面所需的技能，并在1915年获得了承包商资格认证。接下来面临的挑战是如何真正被人雇佣。他在自己的笔记中提到，他穿上了自己最好的西装——那可能也是他唯一一套只在去教堂时穿的西装，拿着他的小公文包，开始挨家挨户敲门。他拜访了当地所有的建筑师，

